# g35-fu-cu core wire fragment

## FEATURE-FACTS: the method-level claim check (protocol hot file host.rs, with mixdog-app-server outgoing.rs)

mcp_surface.rs `ToolBridges::present` now calls `self.host.serves_method(capability, method)` (browser: `host/browser/command`,
visualize: `host/visualize/command`, computer: `host/computer/capture`). The tree compiles only with both of these:

1. mixdog-core-api `src/host.rs`, trait `HostChannel`, right after `fn serves`:

       /// [`HostChannel::serves`] for the one `method` the caller is about to send: a claim that declared `capability` but listed
       /// other methods in its `serves` does not serve it. A channel that cannot tell answers as `serves`.
       fn serves_method(&self, capability: HostCapability, method: Method) -> bool {
           let _ = method;
           self.serves(capability)
       }

2. mixdog-app-server `src/outgoing.rs`, `impl HostChannel for Outgoing`, right after `fn serves`:

       fn serves_method(&self, capability: HostCapability, method: Method) -> bool {
           self.claimant(capability, Some(method)).is_ok()
       }

   Also the same two lines in any other `impl HostChannel` that overrides `serves` (a test double that answers per capability).

## SINGLETONS-CORE: the takeover owner waits for Computer Use to drain

compose_flip.rs real_core: replace

    let takeover = Arc::new(crate::takeover_port::CoreTakeover::new(takeover_holds.clone()));

with (the line after `human_only` is built, as it is now)

    let takeover = Arc::new(crate::takeover_port::CoreTakeover::new(takeover_holds.clone()).with_computer_drain(human_only.clone()));

so a screen takeover's `takeover/ready` waits for the running Computer Use operations as Node's `withHumanOnlyApproval` did.
